    "question_target": "Difference between morphological analysis and morphological inflection."
  },
  "answer": "Morphological analysis and morphological inflection differ in what they take as input and what they produce as output. Morphological analysis starts with a given word and produces its morphosyntactic description, such as a sequence of morphological tags [E1]. Morphological inflection, by contrast, starts with a lemma plus a set of morphological tags and produces the corresponding inflected word form [E2]. So, analysis is essentially word-form-to-tags, while inflection is lemma-plus-tags-to-word-form [E1][E2].",
  "citations": [
    "E1",
    "E2"
  ],
